WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:17.283
Unit thirty-six: Adjective and Noun + Preposition. Today you will use fixed prepositions after adjectives and nouns.

4
00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.340
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.800
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.639
Aware of.

7
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.371
Aware of means knowing about.

8
00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:31.623
She is aware of the risk.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:35.055
Your turn. Say: Aware of.

10
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:38.971
Aware of.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.834
Capable of.

12
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.606
Capable of means able to do.

13
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:45.856
He is capable of more.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.870
Your turn. Say: Capable of.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.804
Capable of.

16
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.748
Reliant on.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.005
Reliant on means depending on.

18
00:00:58.617 --> 00:01:00.419
We are reliant on tourism.

19
00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:03.692
Your turn. Say: Reliant on.

20
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.627
Reliant on.

21
00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:09.651
Reluctance to.

22
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.253
Reluctance to means unwillingness to do.

23
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.548
A reluctance to speak.

24
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.302
Your turn. Say: Reluctance to.

25
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.504
Reluctance to.

26
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.623
Tendency towards.

27
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:29.638
Tendency towards means a habit of moving in a direction.

28
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.099
A tendency towards delay.

29
00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:35.661
Your turn. Say: Tendency towards.

30
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.977
Tendency towards.

31
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:41.857
Insight into.

32
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.337
Insight into means deep understanding of.

33
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.601
An insight into culture.

34
00:01:48.217 --> 00:01:51.206
Your turn. Say: Insight into.

35
00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.451
Insight into.

36
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.473
Impact on.

37
00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:00.332
Impact on means effect on.

38
00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:02.719
The impact on schools.

39
00:02:03.317 --> 00:02:06.155
Your turn. Say: Impact on.

40
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.129
Impact on.

41
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:12.093
Emphasis on.

42
00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:16.058
Emphasis on means special importance given to.

43
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.255
An emphasis on reading.

44
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.468
Your turn. Say: Emphasis on.

45
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.439
Emphasis on.

46
00:02:26.233 --> 00:02:29.687
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:35.011
Visal, which preposition follows impact, insight and emphasis?

48
00:02:36.117 --> 00:02:46.130
Impact on, insight into, emphasis on. Prepositions after nouns and adjectives are fixed, so they must be learned together with the word.

49
00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:48.404
Can you give a group?

50
00:02:49.517 --> 00:03:05.567
Adjectives: aware of, capable of, reliant on, dependent on, sensitive to, responsible for. Nouns: reluctance to, tendency towards, demand for, solution to, reason for, concern about.

51
00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:08.532
What follows the preposition?

52
00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:21.394
A noun or a gerund: She is capable of leading the team. Take care with to: it is a preposition in committed to improving, but an infinitive marker in a reluctance to speak.

53
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:24.312
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:30.133
Grammar focus: Adjective and noun plus fixed preposition plus noun or gerund.

55
00:03:30.433 --> 00:03:31.585
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.283 --> 00:03:33.969
She is aware of the risks.

57
00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:37.521
The report had a major impact on education.

58
00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:40.544
He is capable of leading the team.

59
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:50.059
Learn prepositions with the word: aware of, capable of, reliant on, impact on, insight into, emphasis on, reluctance to, tendency towards.

60
00:03:50.817 --> 00:03:54.526
Be careful! Don't say: She is aware about the risk.

61
00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:58.756
Say: She is aware of the risk.

62
00:03:59.056 --> 00:04:00.139
Use aware of.

63
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.528
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:05.810
Words and Their Partners.

65
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.574
The government is aware of the risks involved.

66
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:12.367
The report had a major impact on education.

67
00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.132
The school places great emphasis on reading.

68
00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.725
There is a tendency towards shorter holidays.

69
00:04:20.733 --> 00:04:23.348
Such combinations must be learned as a unit.

70
00:04:24.433 --> 00:04:28.841
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:29.683 --> 00:04:31.497
She is aware blank the risks.

72
00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:34.719
A, of. B, to. C, with.

73
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:39.964
The answer is A: of.

74
00:04:41.117 --> 00:04:43.383
The impact blank schools was large.

75
00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:46.292
A, at. B, on. C, of.

76
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:51.485
The answer is B: on.

77
00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.359
He is capable blank leading.

78
00:04:54.659 --> 00:04:58.057
A, of. B, for. C, to.

79
00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.135
The answer is A: of.

80
00:05:04.283 --> 00:05:06.051
An insight blank culture.

81
00:05:06.351 --> 00:05:09.923
A, for. B, into. C, about.

82
00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:15.037
The answer is B: into.

83
00:05:16.183 --> 00:05:18.996
According to the reading, what does the school emphasise?

84
00:05:19.296 --> 00:05:22.833
A, reading. B, sport. C, music.

85
00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.030
The answer is A: reading.

86
00:05:29.233 --> 00:05:32.605
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:36.947
Write two sentences with a noun + preposition combination.

88
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.262
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:47.562 --> 00:06:00.132
The new law had a strong impact on small businesses. There is a growing emphasis on environmental education. Both sentences use a fixed noun and preposition combination.

90
00:06:00.432 --> 00:06:02.141
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:09.336
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adjective and noun plus fixed preposition plus noun or gerund.

92
00:06:09.636 --> 00:06:13.740
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

93
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.749
See you in Unit thirty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:18.049 --> 00:06:21.073
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

